{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation","id":1489197,"title":"Nosferatu - sewer orientation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-05T00:56:12-07:00","id":1489197,"title":"Nosferatu - sewer orientation","content":"In our last session (Victorian Age) we went on dodgy quest in the London Sewers to engage the local Nosferatu Brood. While debating rules of engagement and all the usual shit it suddenly dawned on us that as scary as the Nosferatu are on their own turf, they don't have any clan disciplines which'll enable them to actually see, hear or smell better than any mortal down there. <br /> <br /> How do you go about their impaired senses in the sewers?<br /> <br /> V<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;They do say, Mrs. M, that verbal insults hurt more than physical pain. They are of course wrong, as you will soon discover when I stick this toasting fork into your head.&quot;<br /> <br /> --E. Blackadder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24273-vincent","name":"Vincent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24273_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T01:27:58-07:00","id":1489204,"title":"","content":"There are several ways, but first I think it is relevant to keep in mind that generally they won't be engaging in hunting or combat within the sewers. The Nosferatu still hunt above ground more than not, or rely on Animalism, and most of the sewer system is used as transit and escape route, with only the Warren itself being something more. The Warren may be less lit than the above ground, but it is still lit and fitted to have basic conveniences. In Victorian Age London it is possible that the Warren is in an old cave, maybe even at a hidden Mithraeum, connected to the sewers but not a part of them, and even in modern settings it is usually a cave beneath the system.<br /> <br /> So when we talk about the &quot;average&quot; Nosferatu, their needs to navigate the sewers aren't that exceptional. While exploring an unknown passage you'll probably bring light, as you'll do at home, while you're more likely to go in the dark when wandering through known ways. They may even favor tunnels that are usually lit either through grates or by maintenance crew, so they don't have to worry about that as their Obfuscate already takes care of not being seen by such mortals.<br /> <br /> With that, you only really need a select few of them to be actual dark stalkers. One or two members of the Warren may be encouraged to develop such abilities for strategic use, anything else would be left to the quirks of its members, so you may have some Nosferatu that develop Auspex OoC or any other tactic to deal with it, but as a matter of personal development, not a standard clan-wide tactic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T02:36:59-07:00","id":1489208,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answer. Some very good points.<br /> <br /> I cannot help thinking (though rather late in my 27 years of playing the game) that they'd developed Heightened senses or Eyes of the Beast as clan discipline over the years - particularly considering their fondness for the shadows and general occupation in the dark underground.<br /> <br /> V<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;They do say, Mrs. M, that verbal insults hurt more than physical pain. They are of course wrong, as you will soon discover when I stick this toasting fork into your head.&quot;<br /> <br /> --E. Blackadder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24273-vincent","name":"Vincent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24273_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T03:12:29-07:00","id":1489211,"title":"","content":"There are various references to the fact that the Nosferatu transform the sewers into real fortresses and shelters, and I would start from this.<br /> Passages even in the dark are likely to have raised signs that allow them to move easily, hidden passages that lead to comfortable shelters with all the comforts, traps and warning signs, animal ghouls that control every movement, as well as specific points for collapsing entire underground sections and dozens of other ways to buy time.<br /> In the end, what they need is time to organize and respond en masse, and here all their disciplines come in perfect help","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26315-querion","name":"Querion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T05:15:17-07:00","id":1489221,"title":"","content":"I think they know how to navigate it based on skill alone, or use animal ghouls to help them move around in the darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T05:28:21-07:00","id":1489222,"title":"","content":"My theory is that like Gangrel who supposedly live in the wilds, they progress towards that state, they do not begin with it. <br /> <br /> Your average Nosferatu neonate stays above ground. . They're not going to be cassanovas but they can do well with any other feeding style. They have support and inteligence from their seniors to make this an easier process. With the right clothes and makeup, they're not going to live much differently from any other vampire that lacks sex appeal.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu start moving underground because <br /> 1- their growing assets are becoming far flung and they want to move between them secretly without getting into territorial disputes<br /> 2- they start to make enemies as they age. <br /> 3- everyone being clueless about where you live is an advantage both to you and the clan as a whole: nobody knowing how many nosferatu there are is a strength<br /> 4- You can sleep in places people wouldn't even think to explore. <br /> 5-You can store items too hot to handle. <br /> 6- Nosferatu sometimes get uglier as they age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T09:14:57-07:00","id":1489234,"title":"","content":"That's a solid take. The Nosferatu of the Dark Ages didn't find self-segregation among the lepers as aesthetically attractive, they were going where there was no competition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T09:30:57-07:00","id":1489237,"title":"","content":"The Nosferatu are an interesting clan that can be implemented in many different ways which each solve and create various problems.<br /> <br /> If you treat the Nosferatu as a bunch of hackers, then really all you need is a basement within digging range of a communications backbone line. Not much to it other than simply knowing that the warren exists.<br /> <br /> If you treat the Nosferatu as a mixed bag of stock types, like the Warren shown in VtM: Bloodlines, then yeah whatever they can find or modify will make do. Each clan member has a small cubby hole to call their own. The path to get down there will be winding, but most of it will be lit by sanitation lights or other rigged systems. Connection to the surface will be relatively close by since warren members will need to hunt or gather intel for trade.<br /> <br /> Then there is the last way to use the Nosferatu, which is to create a completely separate society underground. Between Potence, Animalism, and mutated animal Ghouls, the Nosferatu can build entire cities underground and at depths that wouldn't interact with most human cities. The access points would be guarded, and guides would accompany coteries to get them up to the levels we normally think of as deep. The abandoned and sealed off train stations we normally think of as a Nosferatu lair would actually be a waypoint to stop off at when going to or returning from the surface. This sort of design that everything below the human made tunnels is completely setup for the Nosferatu to have an advantage.<br /> <br /> Which setup you use determines how much the Nosferatu need help in seeing or knowing their surroundings, though I would point out that Animalism as a clan discipline means you can use animal guides whose senses are sharper than yours to get around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T11:59:09-07:00","id":1489255,"title":"","content":"Clan Disciplines are over rated. Every vampire can learn any Discipline. And they would.<br /> <br /> Because every non-Camarilla clan had a signature Discipline associated with them that no one else had, and they were meant to be antagonists with mystery powers, STs began clamping down on players having access to other Disciplines that weren't &quot;in-clan&quot;. Otherwise you'd have your Camarilla coterie already knowing Obtenebration or Quietus, and the Sabbat and Assamites wouldn't be so mysterious and scary.<br /> <br /> And in LARP, certain powers were much more useful in the artificial constraints of any LARP game. So everyone wanted Potence and Celerity because LARP combat absolutely required you have that. And pretty soon you had vampires regardless of clan all knowing the same stuff. The different clans didn't seem to be different. So many STs there clamped down and issued restrictive rules on what it took to learn out of clan Disciplines. But all it did was slow down players a little bit. But it got many people used to the idea you could only learn your in-clans naturally, and needed something special if you wanted out of clan - other clans to teach you their Disciplines, maybe drinking some blood, or whatever artificial constraints STs try to impose so clan members seem to be from their clan instead of all having Brujah Disciplines.<br /> <br /> But that kind of dynamic only exists in artificial environments like LARP. They don't make sense in the setting. Paying a few points of XP more for an out-of-clan Discipline doesn't make it that much harder to gain a Discipline.<br /> <br /> Naturally tall people are better adapted to play basketball than shorter people. But that does not mean all tall people become NBA players, like basketball, or are even good at basketball; or that shorter people can't ever become good basketball players or even play in the NBA. Having a slight advantage in potential (which is all that an in-clan Discipline is versus an out-of-clan) to develop a skill is not the same as only relying on that skill as opposed to learning other skills.<br /> <br /> So what is my solution to the idea that Nosferatu need a means to see in the dark while they are down in the sewer? Easy, many learn the first rank of Protean if that's what they need. Just like many other vampires also learned it despite not having it in-clan. Protean should not be some &quot;secret&quot; known only to the Gangrel. It's just easier for them to learn, and their clan culture encourages it because they selectively embrace many people who don't live in dense cities and need many of the powers of Protean to survive.<br /> <br /> It's also fine to have some amount of torches, siphoned electricity to power light bulbs, oil lamps, and other artificial light sources inside the warrens. They can have networks of animals they control and instruct to issue warnings to others based on when they notice certain things so the clan gets informed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T18:07:33-07:00","id":1489286,"title":"","content":"Part of the problem is that the entire setup is artificial, many aspects of V:tM are designed not to function. From the Traditions, the faction designs, to the fact that Factions run cities rather than being clan run all boils down to building instability into a system to act as automatic story fodder. Its as much a built in story trope as going to an Inn during a D&amp;D game to start the adventure.<br /> <br /> Be it LARP or Tabletop, the game is always designed to create tension, drama, and stories. Rather than function as a viable simulation of how things would work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T20:11:17-07:00","id":1489297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1489255#post1489255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what is my solution to the idea that Nosferatu need a means to see in the dark while they are down in the sewer? Easy, many learn the first rank of Protean if that's what they need. Just like many other vampires also learned it despite not having it in-clan. Protean should not be some &quot;secret&quot; known only to the Gangrel. It's just easier for them to learn, and their clan culture encourages it because they selectively embrace many people who don't live in dense cities and need many of the powers of Protean to survive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I've always assumed that a sizeable number Nosferatu pick up the first dot of Protean sooner, rather than later. And, in fact, if you go back to pre-modern times, most vampires in general would have ended up getting the first dot of Protean pretty quickly. With vampires only being able to operate at night, and with how (before modern lightning) fire was essentially the only available light source, and then with the fact that open flames can cause R\u00f6tschreck in vampires (there's nothing worse than freaking out and dropping the candle you were trying to light and setting your haven on fire) learning how to see and navigate in the dark without carrying a torch or a candle around with you becomes very, very important.<br /> <br /> These days it's less important and the vast majority of younger, urban dwelling vampires don't bother learning the first dot of Protean. Still, the Nosferatu have a pretty strong clan system, and given where they live I expect that older Nosferatu would encourage younger ones to learn the trick, even if it isn't quite as vital today as it used to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-06T01:47:04-07:00","id":1489301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1489286#post1489286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of the problem is that the entire setup is artificial, many aspects of V:tM are designed not to function. From the Traditions, the faction designs, to the fact that Factions run cities rather than being clan run all boils down to building instability into a system to act as automatic story fodder. Its as much a built in story trope as going to an Inn during a D&amp;D game to start the adventure.<br /> <br /> Be it LARP or Tabletop, the game is always designed to create tension, drama, and stories. Rather than function as a viable simulation of how things would work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. At least if we talk for the series as it was first released. single clan cities would all compete for the same resources so some diversification is necessary. The OG 7 make a lot of sense when it comes to running a city. Well, 5 of them make sense, I'm pretty sure the Gangrel and Brujah continue to exist because they're too difficult to get rid of. But the reality of politics is that things don't work in an ideal way and politicians that manage to get elected are making decisions based on what's best for them not their constituents. If RL politicians really just wanted to do the best for people, humans as a species would have solved hunger and universally exceeded the current developed world's middle class standard of living as technocratic communists, nevermind fixing the housing crisis. Vampires make moves based on what's best for them personally. Upholding messy organizations like the Camarilla is what's best for most vampiric leaders. Tensions/Drama/Stories are the natural result of the vampiric condition. <br /> <br /> Mono-clan cities don't work, unless they're really small cities. <br /> Let's say you're a Toreador. All the vampires in the city are Toreador. They're generalists, so really one of the best examples. <br /> Near everyone wants to feed in the clubs. They're the best places for Toreador. There aren't enough clubs. Lots of fights happen over clubs. <br /> Toreador A befriends Malkavian A. He doesn't want to fight for clubs, he likes hospitals. He can help Toreador A with the clubs so long as TA secures his right to hospitals. <br /> Malkavian A is successful and reproduces. But now Malkavians B and C get into harsh conflicts with other Toreador. They're not good at fighting, so they bring in Brujah... The Brujah can't completely trust the Malkavians, so they bring in Nosferatu, the whole city's a mess, so they bring in the Ventrue.... <br /> <br /> Out of clan alliances are the best way to put yourself above very direct competitors in your own clan. It's natural that vampire society is unstable, it's political.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-06T10:23:46-07:00","id":1489349,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> You didn't actually prove your point, you just stated it was better and then discussed things that don't connect.<br /> <br /> In a single clan city, there is no primogen council, there is no competing clan interests, I won't say there is a lack of politics but I will say there are fewer politics.<br /> <br /> The result of this means that the city and clan is run more like a business/corporation than a community of monsters that try to tolerate each other. If a vampire steps out to line there are a lot fewer hurdles to overcome if there are no factions or clans to negotiate with. Like wise if a mortal is unlikely to maintain the status quo then they would never be considered for the embrace based on clan standards, and with a single clan system you don't have to worry about someone else embracing a problematic mortal which you have to deal with.<br /> <br /> This sort of regimented setup means that rather than have a few dozen vampires hunting every night, you have official feeding houses, rather than hunting grounds. Not to mention that Hunters will have a much harder time isolating a vampire to kill them if they aren't scattered and disunited. Additionally, how much easier would it be for visiting kindred to be kept in pre setup havens rather than just hoping they moved on? The mixed clan city is a logistics nightmare, a single clan city is also a headache, but it has fewer problems.<br /> <br /> In the case of Nosferatu the benefits become even more pronounced. They could have an entire undercity a couple thousand feet below the surface, their herds are the offspring of tunnel people so there is no record of them ever existing, an animal ghoul army worthy of Clan Moulder from Warhammer Fantasy could be on standby, and the surface is watched by specially trained human ghouls and Obfuscated Nosferatu patrols. Anyone who tries to set up shop would be told to leave or the entire clan would crush them.<br /> <br /> If you think about how Vampires function, the need to feed, the avoidance of daylight, and the need to stay hidden, I feel that vampire society would gravitate away from the psuedo-adventure hook design. Would the design be adventure friendly, no of course not, but at the same it wouldn't be stupidly contradictory either.<br /> <br /> A good example of contradictory design is that all vampires are nocturnal predators, all vampires are afraid of fire, only a few clans can see in the dark to some extent, but the electric lightbulb is only about a century and a half old. Technically most if not all vampires wouldn't be able to function in pre-light bulb cities because every single candle flame would run the risk of exposing them due to vampiric freak outs. Most end up hand waving this, but if it ignored that much, it shouldn't be part of the design.<br /> <br /> So how then would vampires' function? Pre-electric lights there wasn't a lot of nighttime travel, especially since technically gas streetlights are open flames. Then add on the concept that in theory there are baying mobs of lupines circling every city just waiting for a random vampire to wander too far from home, despite the fact that a vampire would have a hard time functioning in an old-time city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-06T11:10:33-07:00","id":1489352,"title":"","content":"Your argument hinges on the idea that you need a Primogen council if you have multiple clans. You don't. So it's an argument built upon a fallacy. <br /> <br /> &quot;Primogen council&quot; is just some shlock that got popularized by... Chicago by night I think? Clan Primogen aren't an office mandated by the Camarilla, it's an idea a few cities liked and a few too many authors latched onto it not knowing they could do different. It's not a thing that's going to happen in a city with fewer than 60 vampires. Realistically, you're just going to have the most involved/influential/powerful vampires have meetings, and while titles might be involved there's very rarely going to be political impetus to equally represent clans. A Ventrue, two Toreador, three Brujah, A Nosferatu and a Samedi will likely make a more realistic elder council than one each for BGMNTTV. If all the Malkavians the city are some combination of weak/despised, there's no reason to give them a seat of office. Similarly, with fractious clans like Toreador or Brujah, it's not likely that they are going to want a single representative. .<br /> <br /> Single clan cities are an inherently destructive idea. Parents have a big effect on their kids, grandkids are either spoiled rotten or despised, but great grandkids? cute strangers. Imagine your great-great grandparents/kids travel through time to meet you. What's the connection there? Let's not even get into all the brothers and cousins competing for Grandma's good grace. Now imagine you're all territorial bloodsucking predators who can't all hunt in the same neighbourhood for fear of drawing in hostile forces. You're also all specialized in the same career path when there's limited job openings.... The only bloodline that can do this is the Tremere, and that's because they've got a lot of different ways to specialize. . <br /> <br /> If your city is composed of only Nosferatu, there's not really much purpose in making friends with other Nosferatu. They've largely got the same skills you do. Sure they can OoC and pretend to be Ventrue, but going OoC like that puts them at a disadvantage. Being friends with an Actual Ventrue is just better for the Nosferatu. He's got skills you don't have, he needs skills you have, it's a virtuous relationship. It's simple economics/politics/sociology/whatever. A four Nosferatu team would struggle to compare to a Nosferatu/Ventrue Duo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-06T14:18:41-07:00","id":1489364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1489297#post1489297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, in fact, if you go back to pre-modern times, most vampires in general would have ended up getting the first dot of Protean pretty quickly. With vampires only being able to operate at night, and with how (before modern lightning) fire was essentially the only available light source, and then with the fact that open flames can cause R\u00f6tschreck in vampires (there's nothing worse than freaking out and dropping the candle you were trying to light and setting your haven on fire) learning how to see and navigate in the dark without carrying a torch or a candle around with you becomes very, very important.</div> </div> </div> </div>That actually plays more on the tangent that vampires should have night vision by default than anything else.<br /> <br /> For the Nosferatu I don't think they would have needed Protean more than other vampires, which is the point of the thread. Originally they didn't lived so far in the subterranean, out-of-the-way places was enough. They didn't really needed to hunt and navigate on darker environments than other kindred, as their caves were their houses, not their hunting grounds.<br /> <br /> And while I agree that vampires do develop Out of Clan Disciplines, this is still not feasible as something to expect from most members of a given clan. There's a big difference between a clan expecting a number of its members to learn a given Discipline in a given area, or a given Discipline being common among elders, and an OoC being standard fare among Neonates for basic survival. Indeed, I'd say that not even the whole In-Clan spread should be a necessity. It's imperative in my opinion that any two dots spread among the In-Clans alone should be enough for basic function.<br /> <br /> Was Protean that common in the past? Certainly it wouldn't be hard to find among Ancillae and even some Neonates. But to assume that most vampires had it is against the idea of how hard any Discipline, even an In-Clan, is supposed to be to learn. Going for hard numbers, the XP needed to learn the first dot of a Discipline is more than enough to raise an Ability from 0 to 3, which is the difference between not knowing anything about that and being an actual professional (albeit not a expert) in the field. It's like demanding university-level preparation just to do the basics. Is that a fair demand beyond the starting dots of a Neonate?<br /> <br /> So I agree that night vision should be standard, but as a Discipline it does sound contrived.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-06T16:57:53-07:00","id":1489374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1489352#post1489352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your argument hinges on the idea that you need a Primogen council if you have multiple clans. You don't. So it's an argument built upon a fallacy.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Not even close to my point, please reread and think in bigger picture terms rather than narrative ones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1489352#post1489352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Single clan cities are an inherently destructive idea. Parents have a big effect on their kids, grandkids are either spoiled rotten or despised, but great grandkids? cute strangers. Imagine your great-great grandparents/kids travel through time to meet you. What's the connection there? Let's not even get into all the brothers and cousins competing for Grandma's good grace. Now imagine you're all territorial bloodsucking predators who can't all hunt in the same neighbourhood for fear of drawing in hostile forces. You're also all specialized in the same career path when there's limited job openings.... The only bloodline that can do this is the Tremere, and that's because they've got a lot of different ways to specialize. .</div> </div> </div> </div>1st. May I suggest therapy for that kind of familial outlook.<br /> <br /> 2nd. You have yet to prove that a single clan city is somehow more destructive than a multi-clan city. Everything you can argue is wrong with a single clan city is inherently wrong with a multi-clan one. Rather than having one family under one roof, you have an apartment building of several families all under the same structure and squabbling endlessly.<br /> <br /> 3rd. The Tremere, the Giovanni, the Followers of Set, and to a certain extent the Nosferatu all have relatively speaking, unified clan structures. But the point still stands that there are clans/bloodlines that would absolutely benefit from this sort of setup. Yes this is V20 centric in view, but for my two cents I extremely dislike V5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1489352#post1489352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your city is composed of only Nosferatu, there's not really much purpose in making friends with other Nosferatu. They've largely got the same skills you do. Sure they can OoC and pretend to be Ventrue, but going OoC like that puts them at a disadvantage. Being friends with an Actual Ventrue is just better for the Nosferatu. He's got skills you don't have, he needs skills you have, it's a virtuous relationship. It's simple economics/politics/sociology/whatever. A four Nosferatu team would struggle to compare to a Nosferatu/Ventrue Duo.</div> </div> </div> </div>What a load of BS, who in their right mind thinks that you should never make friends with someone just because they have similar skills? Your entire point is based off of builds rather than experience. A Nosferatu who was an aquaduct designer in ancient Rome will probably have some rather useful knowledge or unlife experience to pass along to the Nosferatu neonate was a mortal sewer worker.<br /> <br /> But since you seem to only value builds, exactly what can a Ventrue do that a Nosferatu can't? Sure there are starter differences, but nosferatu can learn dominate, Obfuscate allows them to hide their countenances, and there is no clan restriction on being competent at business. Its not like the game explicitly says Nosferatu can't be rich or that Ventrue can't be poor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-06T18:52:17-07:00","id":1489379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1489352#post1489352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If your city is composed of only Nosferatu, there's not really much purpose in making friends with other Nosferatu.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue the Niktuku, Lore-wise are enough to keep Nosferatu cooperative. <br /> <br /> And further, not stated in Lore but more headcannon for me: the Nosferatu Founder was a Hunter, likely knew a good bit on animal behavior, and used super high level disciplines to create the Niktuku to keep the clan sharp. Not to destroy them but to cull the unfit.<br /> <br /> And if i remember right, the Independent clans of Revised tended to have single clan base-cities. Buts thats going on decades old memory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T04:59:00-07:00","id":1489407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1489349#post1489349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> You didn't actually prove your point, you just stated it was better and then discussed things that don't connect.<br /> <br /> In a single clan city, there is no primogen council, there is no competing clan interests, I won't say there is a lack of politics but I will say there are fewer politics.<br /> <br /> The result of this means that the city and clan is run more like a business/corporation than a community of monsters that try to tolerate each other. .</div> </div> </div> </div>1: Between stability and profit/growth, most successful Governments choose the latter. In normal circumstances more wealth on the lower end brings stability. More politics is worth it if it brings you more wealth, and since the elders who make the decisions are generally the ones good at politics it stands to reason that most cities will be multi clan. <br /> <br /> 2: A multi-clan city has vampires moving horizontally. &quot;Hey child, go work with the Tremere, you're suffering right now, and it's all the Ventrue's fault&quot;. A single clan city has vampires look vertically. &quot;You have nobody to blame but your grandsire&quot;. While a multi-clan city has constant friction, the breaking point is much higher and the elders have more methods to direct the pent up rage of wronged neonates. A smart leader knows that it's good to divide and rule. Mono-clan cities are short term thinking. Once the family is big enough it's much more dangerous for the leader who doesn't have anyone else to blame. <br /> <br /> 3. Ages being equal, s<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">ingle clan cities will be good targets for stronger, better rounded coteries that are looking for somewhere new to settle down. When you have 20+ Brujah in a city of 1,400,000 all looking for similar feeding things are going to be strained, and one of the best way to win the upcoming conflicts is to look for outside help. <br /> <br /> <br /> With the exception of Assamites who are cheating and have a whole three bloodline caste system to really spread things out, and the versatile yet organized Tremere who both have everything and yet choose to act interdependently, Multi clan cities are the inevitable reality of large cities; while clans like the Tremere and to a lesser extent the Ventrue are built in a way that they can do well on their own without much problems (The Ventrue weakness is literally designed to facilitate internal cooperation) both clans can get much more out of having the other clans in the city. Beyond a certain size, <b>mono-bloodline cities are stupid and wouldn't survive natural selection</b>.<br /> <br /> <i>A necromancer in a city of necromancers has nobody to sell their rare services to and is significantly worse off for it. </i></span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T06:45:24-07:00","id":1489408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1489407#post1489407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beyond a certain size, <b>mono-bloodline cities are stupid and wouldn't survive natural selection</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's absurd. I can't see any reason why any city where the vast majority of members were Nosferatu or Ventrue or Tremere or Toreador would end up with all of the vampires dying. What are you suggesting? That all of the vampires in a Toreador city is going to end up getting into a shootout at the local bar? The Prince will distribute domains accordingly and some vampires will end up with domains they want and some will end up with domains that aren't necessarily their first pick, but that's how it will be in nearly any city because the choice domains are likely already taken and owned by someone.<br /> <br /> Remember that vampires are individuals and frequently vampires will recruit ghouls or even embrace new vampires because of the skills that that ghoul/kindred will bring to the clan. You're probably going to end up with a Toreador who has some experience in the medical field, so hey, he gets the local hospital as his territory. It's really not the sort of existential problem you seem to think it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T08:45:32-07:00","id":1489413,"title":"","content":"Explaining politics to people without the dots... I have no fucking clue how you guys could think mono-clan cities are a more natural state than multi clan cities. <br /> <br /> I can't see any reason why any of the clans, besides the Assamites, would want to maintain a state of one-clan per city. Clans stereotype one another, but very few are actually hostile to one another. Ventrue and Brujah are rivals, but they're not enemies. Toreador and Nosferatu are polar opposites, but they're not enemies. <br /> <br /> Toreador are set up to be fractious. Brujah are set up to be fractious. If you threw an even number of all clans into any city, A Toreador's worst enemies is very likely going to be another Toreador. They have comparable skills. They have similar hunting strategies. They don't really have a weakness that binds them together like a few clans. They don't need one another. They might have a few things that they have in common, they might enjoy eachother's company, but the same could be true for any other clan. Ironically, the Nosferatu and Toreador might have outward distaste from one another, but they make for better neighbours: The Nosferatu doesn't covet the Toreador's club, the Toreador doesn't covet the Nosferatu's warrens. The Toreador isn't likely to enroach on the Nosferatu's spy trade, and the Nos isn't likely to fight for many of the Toreador's friends. <br /> <br /> A Toreador offers another Toreador... slightly different friends. A Nosferatu offers a Nosferatu... it's not much different, assuming similar ages. The Overlap is strong. Meanwhile Toreador and Nosferatu can offer eachother almost everything without much overlap. Pragmatically speaking, A Nosferatu is a better ally for a Toreador than another Toreador. If the city has a shortage of clubs and you're the 9th grandchild of the prince and space is limited, how are you realistically going to get your leg up on your totem pole against equal and more capable rivals? A Nosferatu would be a greater ally than the many Toreador, and if you turn him away, perhaps one of your rivals will make use of him. Potentially it'd be a waste of your resources to chase him away and that would give an advantage to your rivals. <br /> <br /> Imagine you're the patriarch of all the city's Toreador. You need to control your sociopathic kids. They need to control their kids, and they will want kids at some point, they'll get bitter if not allowed. If someone doesn't like something, it's your fault. If someone wants a better status, it's all on you. Nobody's secure in their position/territory, because the positions/attractive territories are limited and everyone is replaceable by the patriarch. Some city essential positions that can't be filled by ghouls aren't well suited for your bloodline and anyone embraced for that position is going to have a difficult time and foster some resentment. If vampires from other clans want to settle in your city, are you really in an ideal position to say no? Mixed coteries will dominate single-clan coteries of a similar age. If mixed coteries lose a political battle in their home city, they will likely find success in taking over mono-clan cities. The clans probably evolved in the first place because specialized divisions of labour and prey types was a better option than non-specialized vampires. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T08:54:02-07:00","id":1489415,"title":"","content":"I think it's important to note that a city of a single clan with the same population will be far less united. There is no reason for the Nosferatu to stick together if everyone in the city is a Nosferatu. Not to mention with greater numbers, you are going to see greater internal division on politics and what not, as it is easier to form cliques. And unlike multi-clan cities, the diverging political views aren't going to be counterbalanced by Clan differences. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1489408#post1489408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that vampires are individuals and frequently vampires will recruit ghouls or even embrace new vampires because of the skills that that ghoul/kindred will bring to the clan. You're probably going to end up with a Toreador who has some experience in the medical field, so hey, he gets the local hospital as his territory. It's really not the sort of existential problem you seem to think it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true, a mono-clan city will see more people diverging from the clan-norms, as they have to specialize in things other clans usually provide. You could even make an argument for how castes originate from this primitive division of &quot;labor&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T09:15:07-07:00","id":1489419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1489413#post1489413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't see any reason why any of the clans, besides the Assamites, would want to maintain a state of one-clan per city. Clans stereotype one another, but very few are actually hostile to one another. Ventrue and Brujah are rivals, but they're not enemies. Toreador and Nosferatu are polar opposites, but they're not enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>This too, there isn't much to be gained. For example lets assume a Ventrue clan-city arises:<ul><li>Elders can no longer play up clan divisions to keep the younger ones divided, being superior by virtue of your Ventrue blood isn't as relevant when everyone is a Ventrue. Fascist regimes, of which a mono-clan city would necessarily be to arise short of extraordinary circumstances, needs external enemies.</li> <li>City becomes a pariah state as the other clans in nearby cities rebuke the idea of being forbidden, expelled or killed for the strengthening of a single clan over others, similarly Ventrue in nearby cities similarly rebuke the idea, as it threatens their position and may warrant retaliatory action against them. They might even lead the efforts against them, in order to mitigate penalties imposed on the clan once that state is torn down.</li> </ul><hr />Also even the Banu Haqim are part of the Ashirra and expectedly share cities with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T10:36:15-07:00","id":1489421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1489407#post1489407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you have 20+ Brujah in a city of 1,400,000 all looking for similar feeding things are going to be strained, and one of the best way to win the upcoming conflicts is to look for outside help.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the stated 1 to 100,000 ratio a city of 1,400,000 would have 14 vampires at the high end, probably fewer. If feeding is strained then they don't allow more vampires to be made, this is the same basic concept that happens in multi-clan cities. So you are not making a point about single clan cities as much as pointing out that population control is required for the masquerade to function, and as I have proven, it is easier to control a single clan than a whole city full of factions and clans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1489407#post1489407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>A necromancer in a city of necromancers has nobody to sell their rare services to and is significantly worse off for it. </i>[/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR]</div> </div> </div> </div>This would only be the case if the necromancers were trying to sell their services to each other rather than specializing and working together. If only we had an in game example of such a thing, like the Giovanni clan running their own city, where the Potence specialists are the enforcers, the Dominate specialists are the bankers and influence peddlers, and the Necromancers are the summoners/research specialists/information gatherers.<br /> <br /> More importantly why does it matter how many necromancers live in a city when they each can have their own unique power structures on top of being a competent necromancer? I have played several Giovanni who were Necromancy focused but ran businesses and had mortal influence. Discipline build does not equal character build, it is just a part of it.<br /> <br /> In a city of one million, that would mean about 10 vampires, also known as about two coteries. That is plenty of feeding space, that is plenty of personal build diversity, and because it is clan vs outsiders that means each individual vampire has more power to draw on than individuals in a multi-clan city. More importantly who in their right mind would seek to attack a city of Necromancers when only Necromancy can fight/combat ghosts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T10:49:49-07:00","id":1489422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1489413#post1489413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Explaining politics to people without the dots... I have no fucking clue how you guys could think mono-clan cities are a more natural state than multi clan cities.<br /> <br /> I can't see any reason why any of the clans, besides the Assamites, would want to maintain a state of one-clan per city. Clans stereotype one another, but very few are actually hostile to one another. Ventrue and Brujah are rivals, but they're not enemies. Toreador and Nosferatu are polar opposites, but they're not enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are thinking almost exclusively in terms of narrative, rather than simulation. In other words, you are talking about the sound of something when the rest of us are talking about the taste of something. Of course, there is going to be a disconnect for you.<br /> <br /> The Brujah and Ventrue were blood enemies, hence the whole Carthage thing. But despite there still being Ventrue and Brujah from that age walking around, the writers handwaved things to be that the two clans are friendly enemies in the same faction. That isn't politics, that is poor writing masquerading as a potential plot hook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T11:55:09-07:00","id":1489423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1489421#post1489421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At the stated 1 to 100,000 ratio a city....</div> </div> </div> </div>I am very aware of the suggestion that's never followed, thank you.<br /> Population pressure is going to be even worse when everyone has the same feeding types. 1:100,000 is under the idea that <i>for the most part</i> the Brujah hang around bars, the Toreador clubs, the Ventrue private venues, the malkavians take up institutions, with Gangrel and Nosferatu around poverty areas. It's not absolute, but it's a strong tendency based on the strengths and weaknesses of each clan. A city that largely concentrates the feeding around one of these areas due to lack of diversity is going to put more strain on these areas. Like , a mono-clan city would probably be pushing it at 1/3rd of the 1/100,000 rule.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This would only be the case if the necromancers were trying to sell their services to each other rather than specializing and working together. </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://media.giphy.com/media/sljlwb80lCjp6/giphy.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If only we had an in game example of such a thing, like the Giovanni clan running their own city, where the Potence specialists are the enforcers, the Dominate specialists are the bankers and influence peddlers, and the Necromancers are the summoners/research specialists/information gatherers. </div> </div> </div>Dominate 3, Sephulcre 5: you've got no more use for other Giovanni. Other clans still have a lot to offer you. You're from a clan of businessmen; the choice is really that simple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 08-07-2022, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T14:13:29-07:00","id":1489426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1489413#post1489413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Explaining politics to people without the dots... I have no fucking clue how you guys could think mono-clan cities are a more natural state than multi clan cities.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>The attitude here is not appreciated. Be respectful of other posters. Take a warning. Also, learn to be less hostile as a whole to posters you disagree with as this is a pattern of behavior.</b></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T03:34:26-07:00","id":1489462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1489413#post1489413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagine you're the patriarch of all the city's Toreador. You need to control your sociopathic kids. They need to control their kids, and they will want kids at some point, they'll get bitter if not allowed. If someone doesn't like something, it's your fault. If someone wants a better status, it's all on you. Nobody's secure in their position/territory, because the positions/attractive territories are limited and everyone is replaceable by the patriarch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Imagine you're the Prince of the city. You need to control the sociopathic vampires. They need to control their kids, and they will want kids at some point, they'll get bitter if not allowed. If someone doesn't like something, it's your fault. If someone wants a better status, it's all on you. Nobody's secure in their position/territory, because the positions/attractive territories are limited and everyone is replaceable by the Prince.<br /> <br /> Whether you're the Prince of a city where most everyone is from your clan or the Prince of a city where nobody is from your clan, it all boils down to the same thing. All the hate and envy and jealousy is going to be directed your way.<br /> <br /> Also note that nobody is (or at least I'm not) saying, &quot;mono-clan cities are are<i> more</i> natural state than multi clan cities.&quot; Just that it's entirely possible that you could see them (if somewhat unlikely) and that ultimately night-to-night activity isn't going to much different than in a more regular city. Meanwhile you're saying that it's literally impossible to have cities composed entirely or chiefly by a single clan because &quot;they wouldn't survive natural selection.&quot; Which, again, is absurd.<br /> <br /> It seems to me that your your position is predicated on the idea that vampires are all basically two-dimension caricatures and that vampires from a Clan are all functionally identical or only capable of doing the same thing. Which I flatly disagree with A Toreador who's into creating electronic music for nightclubs might have very different hobbies and interests than another Toreador that lives further outside of the city and grows living trees into furniture and statues.<br /> <br /> I would expect that any city that has a preponderance of a vampires from a single clan would see a lot more diversity among members of that clan and with many vampires focusing on interests and hobbies that will give them leverage when it comes to dealing with their clanmates. In fact, in such a setting it's entirely plausible that those hobbies and interests will have been a factor that led directly to their embrace in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T04:14:33-07:00","id":1489464,"title":"","content":"Lots of interesting ideas - even if the thread took an unexpected turn.<br /> <br /> I don't really buy the idea of &quot;clan disciplines being over rated&quot; or &quot;they'd probably just developed Protean 1&quot;, 'cause that's not the premise of the game. It's fine by me if people change the premise but I find it interesting in retrospect that they've made 5 editions without even adressing the conundrum. And as mentionened, torches are not easily used by creatures of the night.<br /> <br /> As for the whole mono-clan citites debate, then I'd second AnubisXy's last post - a rather obvious example of a mono-clan city is Vienna in the Dark Ages. I find it very unlikely that the Tremere would tolerate other Clans in their city back then.<br /> As for controlling fledgelings and other obstinate vampires, then revised had a very good description of coterie types, which can put the prince's ability to divide and conquer among vampires into perspective.<br /> <br /> V","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;They do say, Mrs. M, that verbal insults hurt more than physical pain. They are of course wrong, as you will soon discover when I stick this toasting fork into your head.&quot;<br /> <br /> --E. Blackadder","edited":{"userid":24273,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24273-vincent","user":"Vincent","date":". 08-08-2022, 07:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24273-vincent","name":"Vincent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24273_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T04:14:53-07:00","id":1489465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1489286#post1489286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of the problem is that the entire setup is artificial, many aspects of V:tM are designed not to function. From the Traditions, the faction designs, to the fact that <b>Factions run cities rather than being clan run</b> all boils down to building instability into a system to act as automatic story fodder. Its as much a built in story trope as going to an Inn during a D&amp;D game to start the adventure.<br /> <br /> Be it LARP or Tabletop, the game is always designed to create tension, drama, and stories. Rather than function as a viable simulation of how things would work.</div> </div> </div> </div>He said it right here. He believes faction run cities, rather than clan run cities, is fiat born from writers wanting drama and story fodder rather than &quot;how things would work&quot; when realistically that's exactly how it'd work. <i> I can't believe that someone can be so wrong on the internet</i>. <br /> <br /> Natural selection, <i>political selection</i> if I must change the terms I use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 08-08-2022, 07:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T05:42:13-07:00","id":1489472,"title":"","content":"Ehh, I think he's correct insofar as it's logical that if the Camarilla didn't exist then you'd certainly see clans looking to maximize their power over certain cities and territories and doing their best to keep &quot;their&quot; cities and the choicest of domains outside of the hands of other clans. For example I definitely think that the Ventrue would be doing their best to keep the number of vampires from &quot;low clans&quot; to a minimum in their own cities and domains. Which is how things operated before the Camarilla existed. Instead, because of the Camarilla, clans are essentially forced to play nice and share territory and resources with one another.<br /> <br /> When you look at the Dark Ages and earlier settings, you can see that this was sort of a thing, especially with High Clan vampires, which often claimed control over specific geographical territories or areas. Ventrue tended to congregate in Italy and then moved up to Germany after the Roman Empire fell, the Lasombra congregated in the Iberian Peninsula and northern Africa, the Tzimsce congregated in Eastern Europe, the Brujah in northern Africa until Carthage was destroyed, etc. The Cappadocians were the only High Clan that wasn't really tied to a specific geographical range, though they did have a lot of influence in Turkey.<br /> <br /> While not &quot;mono-clans&quot; many of those places ended up as majority-clans where the majority of vampires in that area were from a specific clan, and the rulers of most of the cities in that territory were members of that clan. And if vampires from a different clan attempted to overthrow a leader or take a city, they would often end up drawing the ire of other clanmates and leaders of nearby territories. Those clans controlled most of everything and other vampires were essentially guests in that territory. If clan Ventrue decided they didn't want you in Germany, you probably would not be sticking around for too long.<br /> <br /> These days with the Camarilla, clans aren't really tied to geography the way they used to be, and cities and domains are far more equal than they were in the past. And the point of the Camarilla is that it's the explanation for why modern Kindred society is so much more accepting, diverse and equal than it used to be, because it makes post-Camarilla vampire society more interesting in terms of drama and story fodder than pre-Camarilla vampire society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 08-08-2022, 08:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T06:50:33-07:00","id":1489478,"title":"","content":"Clan-dominated cities would be a natural development simply because people wouldn't travel far and wide just to meet others and build diverse communities on purpose, carefully planning things. And as interesting as Prestation is, the main resources vampires need aren't provided by other vampires, they're provided by mortals. The whole notion that commerce between vampires is fundamental to their existence is preposterous.<br /> <br /> Without outside interference most cities would have evolved from small Domains with a Prince and their Childer, most vampires leaving their sire's territory wouldn't go far, so most areas would be dominated by a given clan. Newcomers from other clans would have to abide to the rule of the dominant monsters and to whatever organization they have for themselves.<br /> <br /> Societies naturally form around ethnicity. Clan is ethnicity. You are what your sire made you to be, nothing else. Context dictates how cities are formed and the people living there learn to adapt instead of magically summoning the perfect set of inhabitants. In this sense (and I'm not agreeing with everything else Thoth says on this matter) he's completely right: the setting encourages multi-clan cities as a thing that doesn't really make much sense from the perspective of simulating natural-like migration patterns, social contact and contract, or the actual needs of the race. It <b>is</b> a Faction-based distribution that <b>is</b> purely a narrative device.<br /> <br /> Like most things about the game, really, because while RL isn't rainbows and shiny unicorns, the level of unavoidable shitty-ness in the setting is just as artificial a narrative device. Or, you know, having blood-feeding magical corpses walking around. I'm not saying that you can't take a few fictional premises and run them at face value to their logical conclusion, you definitely can. But WoD <b>never</b> intended to be such a setting, and trying to tie it to natural rules and say that the setting as-is is the most logical from the perspective of Humanities is both absurd and completely misses the point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T08:50:50-07:00","id":1489486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1489423#post1489423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am very aware of the suggestion that's never followed, thank you.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a suggestion when the books explicitly state the total number of vampires in the world.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Vampire Storyteller's Handbook 3rd Edition</u></b> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;How many vampires are there, anyway?<br /> <br /> From a strictly Cainite point of view, probably around 40,000.<br /> The Middle Kingdom has roughly 20,000 Kuei-jin, for a grand<br /> total of approximately 60,000 \u2013 one for every 100,000 people<br /> on the planet.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Admittedly that number should fluctuate with the mortal population, but in the end if you have an upper limit that means the more vampires you stick in any given city, the fewer total cities will have a vampire presence.<br /> <br /> This gets very interesting when you remember that the world population in 1800 was only about 1 billion rather than our almost 8 billion today, which means the total vampire population would have been about 10,000. This in turn means that if you remove the Kuei-jin portion, then Cainites would be hovering around only 6,600 in total for active, in torpor, or stuck in different dimensions. That is just over 500 members for each of the 13 clans and not counting bloodlines.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1489423#post1489423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dominate 3, Sephulcre 5: you've got no more use for other Giovanni. Other clans still have a lot to offer you. You're from a clan of businessmen; the choice is really that simple.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another thing that is apparently not followed is the requirements for a mortal to become a wraith. Namely the need for a death that would anchor them to this world and a Willpower score of 5 or higher. The number of ghosts running around is bound to be on par or lower than the vampire population, and that is before we discuss if the wraith has stats that are useful. Necromancy while powerful isn't an automatic army builder, so yeah you will need some clan mates to back you up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T11:01:28-07:00","id":1489496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1489486#post1489486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not a suggestion when the books explicitly state the total number of vampires in the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Humans don't spread themselves evenly across the face of the earth, nor can vampires. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is just over 500 members for each of the 13 clans and not counting bloodlines. </div> </div> </div>You think there would be 500 Toreador and 500 Tzmisce? I don't. The more specialized clans are going to be less populous than the more generalized. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another thing that is apparently not followed is the requirements for a mortal to become a wraith. Namely the need for a death that would anchor them to this world and a Willpower score of 5 or higher. The number of ghosts running around is bound to be on par or lower than the vampire population, and that is before we discuss if the wraith has stats that are useful. Necromancy while powerful isn't an automatic army builder, so yeah you will need some clan mates to back you up. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think the core book of VTM does a pretty shitty job in outlining what ghosts can do, but an invisible, intangible informant that most vampires can't deal with is really something worth celebrating. You don't really need Necromancy at it's most generous to do well with Sephulcre. More to the point, a lot of necromancy rituals are really useful and you don't need a ghost to benefit. <br /> <br /> Potence doesn't sync significantly with the Giovanni's other abilities. It's certainly useful and convenient, but often more because the terror it can inspire aids Dominate: One Vamp with Potence 5 is usually less physically perilous than 5 guys with weapons, though there are advantages of disadvantages to both the latter is generally better for &quot;force&quot; and intimidation. Granted, a little out of clan can bolster that Potence, but a Physical-focused Giovanni is really wasting 2 in-clan disciplines. It's not terrible per-say but if you really want a Brute you really are better off getting another bloodline on your side. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T11:05:24-07:00","id":1489497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vincent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1489464#post1489464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really buy the idea of &quot;clan disciplines being over rated&quot; or &quot;they'd probably just developed Protean 1&quot;, 'cause that's not the premise of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea what you mean by this. What &quot;premise&quot; do you think is being violated?<br /> <br /> A player has always been able to pick up an out of clan Discipline at character creation using Freebies. They've always been able to spend XP on out-of-clan Disciplines. <br /> <br /> The earliest example of a setting we have is Chicago By Night which has lots of characters with many out-of-clan Disciplines. In terms of Protean specifically, there are a half dozen characters (non-Gangrel) who have it as an out-of-clan Discipline. Only one of them is Nosferatu, but but at the time CbN was published the idea of Nosferatu all living in the sewers was not really established despite their nickname. <br /> <br /> Only one of the Chicago Nosferatu is said to be living in the sewers. All the others are living somewhere in the surface (Khalid himself lives in some cave north of Evanston where all the other clanmates go for their meetings, but that is not the same thing as living in some underground sewer network). It's not until the clanbook that the trope of them all living in the sewers and having spawning pools becomes a thing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T16:49:02-07:00","id":1489511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1489496#post1489496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humans don't spread themselves evenly across the face of the earth, nor can vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Hence why humans made cities and the vampires in turn followed the food.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1489496#post1489496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You think there would be 500 Toreador and 500 Tzmisce? I don't. The more specialized clans are going to be less populous than the more generalized.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously there will be some wiggle room, but I also think that there will be a higher rate of attrition for several clans. When you factor in Torpor vampires, you could easily lose close to 100 off the top, so active members of a given clan will be even lower.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1489496#post1489496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Potence doesn't sync significantly with the Giovanni's other abilities. It's certainly useful and convenient, but often more because the terror it can inspire aids Dominate: One Vamp with Potence 5 is usually less physically perilous than 5 guys with weapons, though there are advantages of disadvantages to both the latter is generally better for &quot;force&quot; and intimidation. Granted, a little out of clan can bolster that Potence, but a Physical-focused Giovanni is really wasting 2 in-clan disciplines. It's not terrible per-say but if you really want a Brute you really are better off getting another bloodline on your side.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here is a good example of how we look at things differently, a Potence focused Giovanni isn't wasting two in-clan disciplines, because over time there is an upper limit to how much xp you can dump into a discipline without changing generation, eventually they can and will expand to other disciplines. Thats the thing about Vampires, they have all the time in the world to get better at things, the players on the other hand are the reason why games never really last.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T23:30:33-07:00","id":1489535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1489497#post1489497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have no idea what you mean by this. What &quot;premise&quot; do you think is being violated?<br /> <br /> A player has always been able to pick up an out of clan Discipline at character creation using Freebies. They've always been able to spend XP on out-of-clan Disciplines.<br /> <br /> The earliest example of a setting we have is Chicago By Night which has lots of characters with many out-of-clan Disciplines. In terms of Protean specifically, there are a half dozen characters (non-Gangrel) who have it as an out-of-clan Discipline. Only one of them is Nosferatu, but but at the time CbN was published the idea of Nosferatu all living in the sewers was not really established despite their nickname.<br /> <br /> Only one of the Chicago Nosferatu is said to be living in the sewers. All the others are living somewhere in the surface (Khalid himself lives in some cave north of Evanston where all the other clanmates go for their meetings, but that is not the same thing as living in some underground sewer network). It's not until the clanbook that the trope of them all living in the sewers and having spawning pools becomes a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The premise of the various clans is that they each are equiped with a set of supernatural skills which enables them to fulfill their quests in unlife. Toreadors delve into the arts and perfomances. Brujahs revel in combat and strife. Ventrue manipulate and control their fellow vampires. If they hadn't given Toreador Presence, Brujah Potence and Ventrue Dominate, would you tell your players &quot;That's what freebies are for!&quot;?<br /> <br /> If you want to change the premise of this conversation into &quot;Nosferatu don't nest in sewers anyway&quot; then it obviously becomes superfluous. <br /> <br /> V<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;They do say, Mrs. M, that verbal insults hurt more than physical pain. They are of course wrong, as you will soon discover when I stick this toasting fork into your head.&quot;<br /> <br /> --E. Blackadder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24273-vincent","name":"Vincent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24273_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-09T00:50:19-07:00","id":1489536,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Thoth;n1489511][/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR]<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Obviously there will be some wiggle room, but I also think that there will be a higher rate of attrition for several clans. When you factor in Torpor vampires, you could easily lose close to 100 off the top, so active members of a given clan will be even lower. </div> </div> </div>Calling the difference &quot;Wiggle room&quot; is like calling the Pacific a lake. Attrition rate is mostly going to be balanced by higher siring rates. The real factors are how easy it is for different clans to feed, how amiable are they with other clans, and these will in turn influence how many cities the clan inhabits which will further snowball the number of members. &quot;Wiggle room&quot; isn't the right term when it wouldn't be much of a stretch for clans like the Malkavians to probably outnumber pre-nightmares Ravnos by 100-1.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Here is a good example of how we look at things differently, a Potence focused Giovanni isn't wasting two in-clan disciplines, because over time there is an upper limit to how much xp you can dump into a discipline without changing generation, eventually they can and will expand to other disciplines. Thats the thing about Vampires, they have all the time in the world to get better at things, the players on the other hand are the reason why games never really last. </div> </div> </div>A Potence focused Giovanni is worse than a Potence biased Lasombra or a balanced Brujah. Vampires don't have all the time in the world to get better at things. Most die in the first few years, a good chunk within the first few weeks. Mundane skill being equal: If it takes 5 years to create a formidable Giovanni Brute and five months to make an equally formidable Brujah, that might just be twelve times better. Sure when they're both 200 there's not going to be much difference, but at 10 years it'll be stark. The Brujah is much easier to raise and replace. If you want a physical-focused &quot;Enforcer&quot; The Brujah is much better return on investment for elders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 08-09-2022, 03:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-09T02:10:41-07:00","id":1489538,"title":"","content":"With the Giovanni at least, remember that only a handful of them get (officially) sired every decade. Of course the Giovanni embrace more than that but they have to keep the number of new vampires very low each year so that they don't get caught cheating. As such, Giovanni fledgelings are anything but expendable so the clan/family is going to investing into them to make sure that they survive more than a couple of months or weeks. Honestly I'd imagine that the Giovanni probably have, by far, the lowest attrition rate among fledgelings of any vampire clan. If some brute is being embraced into the Giovanni specifically to fill the role of muscle, then it's a safe bet that the family will put plenty of time and resources into his training and education for that role, and that spending 5 or 10 years if it's necessary to help to ensure that they'll be able to fill that role for the next several centuries would be a worthwhile investment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 08-09-2022, 06:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-09T07:00:27-07:00","id":1489548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1489536#post1489536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Calling the difference &quot;Wiggle room&quot; is like calling the Pacific a lake. Attrition rate is mostly going to be balanced by higher siring rates. The real factors are how easy it is for different clans to feed, how amiable are they with other clans, and these will in turn influence how many cities the clan inhabits which will further snowball the number of members. &quot;Wiggle room&quot; isn't the right term when it wouldn't be much of a stretch for clans like the Malkavians to probably outnumber pre-nightmares Ravnos by 100-1.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wiggle room is quite accurate when the difference is only a couple hundred members or so, especially when that 500 per clan breakdown didn't include bloodlines, which means clans probably had closer to 450 as the baseline.<br /> <br /> As for Feeding = clan size, once again this is where the Narrative approach and Simulation approach differ. The game wants the narrative of the vampire waking up and hunting almost every night. But the game also gives you the option for a Herd background, which more or less negates the idea of hunting as a baseline activity.<br /> <br /> Any Clan or Bloodline that benefits from a stable location and the resources to maintain it, would greatly benefit from avoiding hunting and investing in Herd. The clans that can't socialize, don't have controlling powers, can't build wealth, or are just too mobile to create herds would prioritize hunting.<br /> <br /> As for Malks vs Ravnos numbers, both clans have weaknesses that intrinsically make for very high attrition numbers, occasionally at the hands of their own coterie members. Between Fish Malks and Kender with Fangs, both are real headaches. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1489536#post1489536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Potence focused Giovanni is worse than a Potence biased Lasombra or a balanced Brujah. Vampires don't have all the time in the world to get better at things. Most die in the first few years, a good chunk within the first few weeks. Mundane skill being equal: If it takes 5 years to create a formidable Giovanni Brute and five months to make an equally formidable Brujah, that might just be twelve times better. Sure when they're both 200 there's not going to be much difference, but at 10 years it'll be stark. The Brujah is much easier to raise and replace. If you want a physical-focused &quot;Enforcer&quot; The Brujah is much better return on investment for elders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again you are not taking the complete picture into account. The Brujah clan weakness means that they are always going to be easier to anger and as a result bait out. Thus on a tactical level while the Brujah might have stronger starting discipline line up, their clan weakness makes them far less desirable, especially if you are trying to keep things some what covert.<br /> <br /> Also where are you getting the 5 years vs five months numbers? If we assume that they have identical starter abilities and attributes for the sake of simplicity, and we assume they both sunk all three starter dots into Potence, why does one clan take years to grind the xp for the last two dots while the other only takes months?<br /> <br /> Alternatively both could have burned the majority of bonus points at creation and just gotten the last two dots, which means they start at Potence 5 and everything after that point is a question of using XP to fill in the other stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-09T13:02:19-07:00","id":1489579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1489548#post1489548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wiggle room is quite accurate when the difference is only a couple hundred members or so, especially when that 500 per clan breakdown didn't include bloodlines, which means clans probably had closer to 450 as the baseline.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Any Clan or Bloodline that benefits from a stable location and the resources to maintain it, would greatly benefit from avoiding hunting and investing in Herd. The clans that can't socialize, don't have controlling powers, can't build wealth, or are just too mobile to create herds would prioritize hunting. </div> </div> </div> Ravnos are neither geared towards hunting nor building the wealth to build herd. (dominate) Malkavians excel at both, . The clans are not built equally. They are all built to survive, but not always to thrive. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Once again you are not taking the complete picture into account. The Brujah clan weakness...</div> </div> </div> </div> Who's not looking at the complete picture here? Brujah are an example. The <i>majority</i> of clans make better dedicated muscle (Give them a name and adress and they'll get the guy for you) than the Giovanni. Assamites, Brujah, Gangrel, Lasombra. Nosferatu, Ravnos, Toreador, Tremere. We can argue if they're better than Ventrue. The Malks are worse unless you want your enemies dead or torpored without warning, and Tzmisce muscle really isn't something you should be trying to use in cities. .If we're talking policing more generally, with investigation required to find kindred in hiding, the Giovanni are good.... so long as you spread the disciplines out.<br /> <br /> Perhaps we're too fixated on Gios. But they really are a clan that's best using all skills in tandem rather than fixating on one. With only one discipline in each major area, they don't excel physically. They don't excel socially, they've got a very narrow focus mentally. These abilities sync well together in gathering backgrounds, and that's their best strength. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also where are you getting the 5 years vs five months numbers... </div> </div> </div> Of course i'm making that up. Even of we compare XP costs the and assume OoC is 40% slower the value of having 4 potence vs 3 potence 2 celerity isn't something easy to answer. Nor can we really find a good way to give a good XP accumulation rate for the years a slightly more active vampire would get, Do they get 1 xp a month, a year? 3-10xp every weekly case they complete? <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alternatively both could have burned the majority of bonus points at creation and just gotten the last two dots, which means they start at Potence 5 and everything after that point is a question of using XP to fill in the other stuff. </div> </div> </div> ,,,, Players really are special cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-09T14:47:04-07:00","id":1489584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vincent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1489535#post1489535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The premise of the various clans is that they each are equiped with a set of supernatural skills which enables them to fulfill their quests in unlife.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see what you mean now. But I don't agree that is the premise of the various clans. I have never heard anyone articulate the clans in that way. Now of course to a certain degree the game did align the in-clan Disciplines for the general concept of the clan. But that doesn't mean the members of those clans have a specific &quot;quest in unlife&quot; to fulfill. Clans don't have quests. And individual vampires determine their own activities, they don't simply become robots programmed with some quest just because that is their clan.<br /> <br /> At best one can say clans approximate certain Archetypes and their set of in-clan Disciplines lean towards those Archetypes. But they were never meant to be limiting or provide all the tools a vampire would need.<br /> <br /> But regardless of how you word it, I still don't see how that's a problem for the Nosferatu as a whole.<br /> <br /> First, &quot;they live in sewers&quot; is neither an archetype or a quest. <br /> <br /> Second, these vampires existed long before sewers were a thing. Primitive drainage systems might have provided sanitation for the earliest cities, but they wouldn't have given Nosferatu anywhere to hide. Classical civilizations like Rome did have more extensive sewer systems, but they weren't like the modern sanitation systems that only developed in the 19th century. Only a few cities like Rome itself probably had extensive and large enough tunnels to accommodate hiding places. Most historical Nosferatu would not have had any sewer systems at all. The clan has to be more than that.<br /> <br /> Third, we do have two archetypes for the Nosferatu - the meta one and the one in game. The meta one is simple - it's the 1922 German silent movie Nosferatu and the derivatives from that image (such as the 1979 remake, the vampire in the 1979 TV miniseries Salem's Lot TV). From that we get the idea of a vampire that looks inhuman and a vague suggestion of a rodent because of the position of the fangs and an association with a plague. There are no ties to sewers, but the ratlike features and the plague's association with rats do lend itself to Animalism. The one in game is simpler - Nosferatu is supposed to be a great hunter, and the clan's Disciplines lend itself very well to that. Combined with the more monstrous depiction of that clan's vampires, the best description of the Nosferatu is that it is a clan of monsters that humanity does not know is there so it needs places to hide. The key power here is Obfuscate. The Nosferatu need to hide or disguise themselves. A sewer is simply another place for those monsters to hide (and associated with rats which is another Nosferatu theme), but not the only one. It becomes an emergent idea once modern sewer systems become installed, especially when combined with urban legends about flushing baby alligators and other animals down the toilet that then grow to enormous size as that lends itself to their Animalism power.<br /> <br /> I think it's perfectly find to go with that association. It's a strong one. I like it too. But I disagree that even on an archetypal basis that Nosferatu buying an out-of-clan Discipline to see in the dark somehow violates &quot;the premise of the game.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vincent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1489535#post1489535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to change the premise of this conversation into &quot;Nosferatu don't nest in sewers anyway&quot; then it obviously becomes superfluous.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not changing the premise of the conversation. I'm saying that I think your premise of the clan, or premise of the game, is wrong.<br /> <br /> There are various ways a Nosferatu could navigate a secret &quot;kingdom&quot; underground. But buying the first level of Protean at out-of-clan XP costs would probably be the best one, even if it is not the only one. And the Nosferatu who decide to lair on the surface elsewhere don't need to buy it at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-09T23:15:37-07:00","id":1489609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1489584#post1489584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are various ways a Nosferatu could navigate a secret &quot;kingdom&quot; underground. But buying the first level of Protean at out-of-clan XP costs would probably be the best one, even if it is not the only one. And the Nosferatu who decide to lair on the surface elsewhere don't need to buy it at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a good point and very much answers my initial question on how you go about it.<br /> <br /> I can see how my use of the phrase &quot;premise of the game/clan&quot; quickly became both constricting and generic at the same time, and I agree with your point on how sewers is a fairly novel playground for the clan. My point was merely that if you have a clan so disfiguered that it needs to operate in the dark, wouldn't it be prudent for them to actually be able to see in the dark? Hence my wondering why heightened senses/eyes of the beast isn't a clandiscipline of theirs. But I believe we've covered the topic sufficiently.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the input.<br /> <br /> V<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;They do say, Mrs. M, that verbal insults hurt more than physical pain. They are of course wrong, as you will soon discover when I stick this toasting fork into your head.&quot;<br /> <br /> --E. Blackadder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24273-vincent","name":"Vincent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24273_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T01:08:06-07:00","id":1492790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1489421#post1489421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At the stated 1 to 100,000 ratio a city of 1,400,000 would have 14 vampires at the high end, probably fewer. If feeding is strained then they don't allow more vampires to be made, this is the same basic concept that happens in multi-clan cities. So you are not making a point about single clan cities as much as pointing out that population control is required for the masquerade to function, and as I have proven, it is easier to control a single clan than a whole city full of factions and clans.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> In a city of one million, that would mean about 10 vampires, also known as about two coteries. That is plenty of feeding space, that is plenty of personal build diversity, and because it is clan vs outsiders that means each individual vampire has more power to draw on than individuals in a multi-clan city. More importantly who in their right mind would seek to attack a city of Necromancers when only Necromancy can fight/combat ghosts?</div> </div> </div> </div>The numbers of vampires to make their society work with a prince, primogen council, sheriff, harpy, etc only work if the number is 1 in 50k. That way a city like St. Louis or Pittsburgh can have 50~60 vampires if we take into account the metro population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T06:17:18-07:00","id":1492797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1492790#post1492790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The numbers of vampires to make their society work with a prince, primogen council, sheriff, harpy, etc only work if the number is 1 in 50k. That way a city like St. Louis or Pittsburgh can have 50~60 vampires if we take into account the metro population.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume that only the largest cities have all those positions and most have only a few. I love 1st and 2nd edition city books, when every city had a slightly different structure, instead of the copy/paste feeling that later sourcebooks created. Even Chicago by night 1st edition had just a Prince, 6 Promogens and a Sheriff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T06:31:53-07:00","id":1492798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1489472#post1489472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ehh, I think he's correct insofar as it's logical that if the Camarilla didn't exist then you'd certainly see clans looking to maximize their power over certain cities and territories and doing their best to keep &quot;their&quot; cities and the choicest of domains outside of the hands of other clans. For example I definitely think that the Ventrue would be doing their best to keep the number of vampires from &quot;low clans&quot; to a minimum in their own cities and domains. Which is how things operated before the Camarilla existed. Instead, because of the Camarilla, clans are essentially forced to play nice and share territory and resources with one another.<br /> <br /> When you look at the Dark Ages and earlier settings, you can see that this was sort of a thing, especially with High Clan vampires, which often claimed control over specific geographical territories or areas. Ventrue tended to congregate in Italy and then moved up to Germany after the Roman Empire fell, the Lasombra congregated in the Iberian Peninsula and northern Africa, the Tzimsce congregated in Eastern Europe, the Brujah in northern Africa until Carthage was destroyed, etc. The Cappadocians were the only High Clan that wasn't really tied to a specific geographical range, though they did have a lot of influence in Turkey.<br /> <br /> While not &quot;mono-clans&quot; many of those places ended up as majority-clans where the majority of vampires in that area were from a specific clan, and the rulers of most of the cities in that territory were members of that clan. And if vampires from a different clan attempted to overthrow a leader or take a city, they would often end up drawing the ire of other clanmates and leaders of nearby territories. Those clans controlled most of everything and other vampires were essentially guests in that territory. If clan Ventrue decided they didn't want you in Germany, you probably would not be sticking around for too long.<br /> <br /> These days with the Camarilla, clans aren't really tied to geography the way they used to be, and cities and domains are far more equal than they were in the past. And the point of the Camarilla is that it's the explanation for why modern Kindred society is so much more accepting, diverse and equal than it used to be, because it makes post-Camarilla vampire society more interesting in terms of drama and story fodder than pre-Camarilla vampire society.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of that is also that the meaning of a &quot;clan&quot; has changed over time. In the earliest days, a clan meant a family composed of an Antedeluvian, its children and grandchildren. As generations spread and the ancients spent more and more time sleeping, &quot;clan&quot; gradually changed to mean &quot;race&quot;. You're no longer a member of the family of Arikel, you're a member of the Toreador race.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T08:04:25-07:00","id":1492804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1492797#post1492797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume that only the largest cities have all those positions and most have only a few. I love 1st and 2nd edition city books, when every city had a slightly different structure, instead of the copy/paste feeling that later sourcebooks created. Even Chicago by night 1st edition had just a Prince, 6 Promogens and a Sheriff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention that in some places there may be vampires that hold more than one title, as they have more than one function. And in some the whole idea may be that as many vampires as possible get some official title to position them in the social structure. The idea that all the titles in the book exist, and at the same time represent only a bureaucratic ruling class, while easy to conclude is an assumption completely uneeded.<br /> <br /> It wouldn't harm, though, if the books exemplified those two extreme situations to better drive home what they already explicitly say (because as much as people insist on assuming this, the books <b>always</b>, <b>repeatedly</b> state that those titles shouldn't be taken at face value as a standard).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T08:13:12-07:00","id":1492805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1492798#post1492798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of that is also that the meaning of a &quot;clan&quot; has changed over time. In the earliest days, a clan meant a family composed of an Antedeluvian, its children and grandchildren. As generations spread and the ancients spent more and more time sleeping, &quot;clan&quot; gradually changed to mean &quot;race&quot;. You're no longer a member of the family of Arikel, you're a member of the Toreador race.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very good observation! Indeed, that's an extremely subtle distinction, but also very important.<br /> <br /> While the list of clans and the means to be considered a member may not have changed (or changed due to specific circumstances), the underlying meaning of &quot;clan&quot; changed considerably. From nuclear family to extended family, then to a kind of noble house, then a nationality of sorts, then an ethnicity with ever-changing relevance on what it means to belong to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T11:37:48-07:00","id":1492905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489197-nosferatu-sewer-orientation?p=1492790#post1492790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The numbers of vampires to make their society work with a prince, primogen council, sheriff, harpy, etc only work if the number is 1 in 50k. That way a city like St. Louis or Pittsburgh can have 50~60 vampires if we take into account the metro population.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, it works if we assume that Vampire control half as much territory worldwide as we do currently, thus the few cities with a vampire presence can have the numbers you are talking about. But when storytelling a given game, it is far too easy to forget how significant a vampire population you are actually using.<br /> <br /> VtM is a headache because it wants to have a limited vampire population that is simultaneously everywhere and restricted to large cities. All the while not really having a functional restriction on reproduction, but not addressing the fact that vampires could out embrace practically any amount of attrition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}